# Tirvona Yatra — staging configuration template
#
# Copy this file to  Newbackend/.env.staging  (already ignored by git) and fill it in yourself.
# Do NOT paste these values into chat. The staging kit reads them from the file and never prints them.
#
# Every value must belong to a SEPARATE staging / test account. The kit refuses to run if anything
# matches the live configuration in Newbackend/.env (same database or Supabase project, live Razorpay
# keys, same Cloudinary cloud or key, same Resend key).

# 1. A NEW Supabase project used only for staging (Supabase dashboard → New project).
#    Project Settings → Database → Connection string. Use the "Session pooler" (port 5432) or the
#    direct connection (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432), not the transaction pooler.
STAGING_SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# 2. Razorpay TEST mode (Razorpay dashboard → switch to Test Mode → Account & Settings → API keys).
#    The key id MUST start with rzp_test_. Webhook secret: any random string (the kit signs its own
#    webhook deliveries with it; Razorpay cannot reach a local machine).
STAGING_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
STAGING_RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
STAGING_RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# 3. A separate Cloudinary account (or a separate product environment) for staging.
#    Dashboard → Product Environment Credentials.
STAGING_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
STAGING_CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
STAGING_CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# 4. Resend: a staging API key (Resend → API Keys → Create, "Sending access") and a verified sender.
#    STAGING_TEST_EMAIL_TO must be a mailbox you can read; staging emails go only there.
STAGING_RESEND_API_KEY=
STAGING_RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=
STAGING_TEST_EMAIL_TO=

# Then run, from D:\desktop\tirvona-main\tirvona-main :
#   node docs/tirvona-yatra/staging/tools/yatra-staging-check.mjs preflight
#   node docs/tirvona-yatra/staging/tools/yatra-staging-check.mjs db
#   node docs/tirvona-yatra/staging/tools/yatra-staging-check.mjs services
#   node docs/tirvona-yatra/staging/tools/yatra-staging-check.mjs e2e      (one manual Razorpay TEST checkout)
